title: Women's Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and womens_rights_timer = 0 and chancellor_party == "SPD"
on-arrival: womens_rights_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/PfülfAntonie.jpg
frequency: 50
max-visits: 6

= Women's Rights

The Basic Law says that men and women are equal, but women in Germany still earn about 16% less than men, do most of the unpaid care work, and make up only a third of the Bundestag. Abortion is still in the criminal code under Paragraph 218.

- @labor: Close the pay gap.
- @family: Introduce a parity law for elections.
- @welfare: Expand childcare and parental allowance.
- @liberalize: Take abortion out of the criminal code.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@labor
subtitle: Pay transparency, equal pay audits and the right to return to full-time work.
on-arrival: womens_work += 1; womens_rights += 1; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1 - dissent); fdp_relation -= 2; economic_growth += 0.1;
max-visits: 3

Companies must now publish what they pay, and women can see whether they are paid less than male colleagues. Employers complain about the paperwork.

@family
subtitle: Party lists and constituencies must alternate between women and men.
on-arrival: family_law += 1; womens_rights += 1; new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 2; coalition_dissent += 1; cdu_relation -= 4; afd_relation -= 3
max-visits: 2

The Constitutional Court struck down parity laws in Thuringia and Brandenburg, so we write it more carefully this time. The Union and the AfD say that voters, not quotas, should decide.

@welfare
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: welfare += 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); budget -= 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare >= 1 and unemployment_rate >= 8; unemployment_rate -= 0.2; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth += 0.3;

We fund more childcare places and raise the parental allowance for the first time since 2007. [? if welfare >= 1 and unemployment_rate >= 8 : Some of our coalition partners say that we cannot afford this now. ?]

@liberalize
max-visits: 1
subtitle: [? if progressive_coalition < 50 : This is unlikely to succeed; we do not have majority support. ?]
go-to: liberalize_fail if progressive_coalition < 50; liberalize_success if progressive_coalition >= 50

@liberalize_fail
on-arrival: cdu_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1; new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent);

Our bill fails in the Bundestag. The Union threatens to go to the Constitutional Court, and a few of our own members vote against it. The campaigners will try again.

@liberalize_success
on-arrival: abortion_rights += 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1; cdu_relation -= 8; rural_spd -= 2; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); catholics_spd += 2*(1-dissent)

With the Grüne and the Linke, we pass a law that makes abortion in the first twelve weeks legal, outside the criminal code. Most Germans support it, but the Union and the churches are angry, and the Union announces a challenge at the Constitutional Court.
